// Somewhere to stop that is not stopping: the machine stays alive so a
// screenshot has something to photograph. The shell replaces it.
//
// The counter is a `word` and never changes. It was an `int` being incremented,
// which reached two billion in about a second, wrapped negative, left the loop
// and powered the machine off -- so every screenshot came back empty and the
// hold looked like it was working.
hold() {
  word spins = 0;
  while(spins >= 0) {
    cpu_halt();
  }
} return void;
